  "notes": "PoE, read 2026-11-28. `https://dl.ui.com/ds/usw-48_ds.pdf` (HTTP 200, `application/pdf`, 2,599,051 B, text layer) prints **Networking Interfaces = (48) 10/100/1000 Mbps Ethernet RJ45 Ports / (4) 1 Gbps SFP Ports**, **Power Method = Universal AC Input: 100-240VAC, 50/60 Hz**, **Power Supply = AC/DC, Internal, 60W** and **Max. Power Consumption = 40W**. Nothing on the sheet sources or sinks PoE: this is the non-PoE UniFi Switch 48. Its 48 copper ports carry `poeIn: false` because `isPoePd()` matched `unifi` in the label (\\\"UniFi Switch 48\\\") and inferred 12.95 W on each - 621.6 W drawn from a PSE by a switch on an internal 60 W AC supply."
